\b St. Dominic Care\b0\par
\b 14. Site Super User designation\b0\par
\par
This form names the people who own day-to-day use of the St. Dominic Care system at this site. It is not valid until both names are written in by site leadership and the form is signed. No Super User is named in the software repository.\par
\par
\b Site\b0\par
St. Dominic Care\par
\par
\b Primary Super User\b0\par
Name: ________________________________\par
Role / department: ________________________________\par
Contact: ________________________________\par
\par
\b Backup Super User\b0\par
Name: ________________________________\par
Role / department: ________________________________\par
Contact: ________________________________\par
Acts when the primary Super User is absent, on leave, or unreachable.\par
\par
\b Escalation path\b0\par
1. Staff member reports the problem to the shift or department lead.\par
2. Department lead contacts the Primary Super User.\par
3. If the Primary Super User is unavailable, contact the Backup Super User.\par
4. Access, role, or account problems go to an Administrator (Admin role; authenticator required at /admin/security).\par
5. Medical-record or audit questions go to the Records Officer who owns the audit trail.\par
6. If the system is down or data may have been exposed, the Super User notifies the Administrator and site leadership the same day. Do not wait for the next business day.\par
\par
\b Duties\b0\par
The Super User is the first contact for how to use the system, password resets that need an admin, and reporting outages. The Super User does not replace clinical judgment or the Records Officer's audit review.\par
\par
\b Sign-off\b0\par
Designated by: ________________________________  Date: ______________\par
Primary Super User signature: ________________________________\par
Backup Super User signature: ________________________________\par
}
